# Level 4: Counterweight Row
# Use the boulder as mobile cover, drop it through the weak floor, then roll it
# along the lower service lane onto the counterweight plate.
script counterweight_row
playerStart 78 140

# Full-height chamber shell.
solid 0 0 1600 28
solid 0 28 28 152

# Start balcony and one continuous inclined ramp. The ramp's upper surface meets
# both adjoining platforms within two pixels, so visual and physics edges agree.
solid 0 180 370 32
ramp 518 282 360 32 30
platform 680 360 170 32

# First descent: ramp landing to the firing-gallery floor.
ladder 780 350 44 210
solid 620 560 200 40

# A compact spike shaft separates the entry landing from the puzzle gallery.
# spikePitTop keeps its visible masonry walls aligned with the y=560 platforms.
spikePitTop 560
spikeHazard 820 773 80 32

# Upper firing gallery. The boulder blocks arrows while it is pushed right.
# Its weight cracks the center bridge and drops it into the service lane.
# The near ladder occupies a real opening between these two gallery sections.
platform 900 560 95 32
platform 1039 560 161 32
breakableTile 1200 560 100 32 0.65
# The far ladder has a matching opening immediately to the right of the exit.
platform 1300 560 250 32
arrowTrap 1318 500 -1 0 1.30 500
arrowTrap 1318 540 -1 0 1.65 455
boulder 1135 520 28 3.4

# Lower counterweight lane. The near ladder lets the player follow the fallen
# boulder; the far ladder returns them beside the now-open exit.
solid 932 600 32 300
solid 964 820 636 80
ladder 995 520 44 300
ladder 1550 520 40 300
button 1435 808 92 16

# Wide enough for the player sprite and multiplayer characters to enter cleanly.
exit 1415 340 120 220
